CVA6ConfigDcacheSetAssoc = 8 Signal Flow Tree (32KB 8-way Configuration)
========================================================================

1. CONFIGURATION PHASE (cv32a6_imac_sv32_config_pkg.sv)
   └── localparam CVA6ConfigDcacheSetAssoc = 8;
       └── cva6_cfg.'{ DcacheSetAssoc: unsigned'(CVA6ConfigDcacheSetAssoc) }

2. BUILD/DERIVATION PHASE (build_config_pkg.sv)
   └── CVA6Cfg.DcacheSetAssoc = 8
       ├── DCACHE_SET_ASSOC = CVA6Cfg.DcacheSetAssoc = 8
       ├── DCACHE_SET_ASSOC_WIDTH calculation:
       │   └── CVA6Cfg.DcacheSetAssoc > 1 ? $clog2(CVA6Cfg.DcacheSetAssoc) : CVA6Cfg.DcacheSetAssoc
       │       └── $clog2(8) = 3 bits
       │
       └── Used in INDEX_WIDTH calculation:
           └── $clog2(CVA6Cfg.DcacheByteSize / CVA6Cfg.DcacheSetAssoc)
               └── $clog2(32768 / 8) = $clog2(4096) = 12 bits

3. MODULE INSTANTIATION PHASE
   └── std_cache_subsystem (core/cache_subsystem/std_cache_subsystem.sv)
       └── wt_dcache (core/cache_subsystem/wt_dcache.sv)
           └── wt_dcache_mem (core/cache_subsystem/wt_dcache_mem.sv)
               └── parameter DCACHE_SET_ASSOC = CONFIG.DCACHE_SET_ASSOC = 8

4. MEMORY ARRAY GENERATION
   └── SRAM Array Generation (wt_dcache_mem.sv)
       └── for (genvar i = 0; i < DCACHE_SET_ASSOC; i++)
           ├── Generate 8 SRAM instances (one per way)
           ├── Each SRAM: NUM_WORDS = 256, DATA_WIDTH = DCACHE_LINE_WIDTH
           └── Array indexing: cl_data_way[i], cl_tag_way[i], cl_vld_way[i]

5. ASSOCIATIVITY LOGIC IMPACT
   └── Way Selection and Comparison:
       ├── Tag comparison across 8 ways in parallel
       ├── Hit detection: hit_way[DCACHE_SET_ASSOC-1:0] → hit_way[7:0]
       ├── LRU replacement policy across 8 ways:
       │   └── plru_tree_i #(.ENTRIES(DCACHE_SET_ASSOC))
       │       └── 8-way PLRU tree for replacement selection
       │
       └── Way multiplexing:
           ├── rd_data_way[7:0] selection for read hits
           └── wr_way_sel[7:0] for write operations

6. HARDWARE COMPLEXITY
   └── 8-way Associative Implementation:
       ├── 8 tag comparators (parallel comparison)
       ├── 8:1 data multiplexer for read selection
       ├── 3-level PLRU tree (log2(8) = 3)
       ├── 8 valid bit checks
       └── Moderate hardware overhead

7. SIGNAL WIDTH IMPACT
   └── Associativity-related signals:
       ├── hit_way[DCACHE_SET_ASSOC-1:0] → hit_way[7:0]
       ├── way_sel[DCACHE_SET_ASSOC_WIDTH-1:0] → way_sel[2:0]
       ├── plru_way[DCACHE_SET_ASSOC_WIDTH-1:0] → plru_way[2:0]
       └── cl_vld_way[DCACHE_SET_ASSOC-1:0] → cl_vld_way[7:0]

8. PERFORMANCE CHARACTERISTICS
   └── 8-way Associativity Benefits:
       ├── Good conflict miss reduction
       ├── Reasonable hardware complexity
       ├── Fast way selection (3-bit encoding)
       ├── Efficient PLRU implementation
       └── Industry-standard configuration

9. COMPARISON WITH FA CACHE
   └── 8-way vs Fully Associative:
       ├── 8-way: 256 sets × 8 ways = 2048 lines
       ├── FA would be: 1 set × 2048 ways
       ├── 8-way has much lower hardware complexity
       ├── 8-way has slightly higher conflict misses
       └── 8-way has faster access time

KEY RELATIONSHIPS:
- DcacheSetAssoc = 8 creates conventional 8-way set-associative cache
- Balanced design: good hit rate without excessive hardware
- Each way contains 4KB (32KB / 8 ways)
- Way selection requires only 3 bits
- Standard configuration proven in many designs